invariant: INV-14
file: srv_auth.c
catches: srv_auth_test
reason: a signer that refused may have written part of a signature into
  the caller's buffer, and this drops the wipe that clears it. The length
  still reports zero, so a caller that read the buffer without reading
  the return code would put those bytes in a CertificateVerify.
  test/srv_auth_test.c signs with a scalar above the group order, which
  p256_sign refuses, and requires every byte of the buffer to be zero
  afterwards.

--- old
        ct_wipe(sig, cap);
        *sig_len = 0;
--- new
        *sig_len = 0;
